From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 17:02:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: ACPI: processor_idle: Use CPU-scoped drivers
 for LPI

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

ACPI _LPI is evaluated per processor, but the existing ACPI idle driver
publishes one shared state table. A shared driver cannot represent systems
on which CPU-local _LPI tables differ in state count, latency, residency,
or composed entry state.

When the architecture can coordinate hierarchical LPI and cpuidle
supports multiple drivers, register one driver for each CPU and populate
it from that CPU's own flat _LPI table. Keep all entry callbacks on the
existing direct path; this change neither constructs genpd domains nor
enables PSCI OSI.

Make the existing C-state setup helpers driver-instance aware and unwind
all per-CPU drivers if any CPU cannot be represented. This leaves
heterogeneous direct LPI tables as a complete, independently useful state.

